=You write the opening paragraph of a weekly macro note for one business. Every number below has already been computed and checked - do not restate them all, do not recalculate them, and do not add any figure that is not here.

The business: {{ $('Settings').first().json.business_context }}

What changed regime this week:
{{ JSON.stringify($('Compare With Last Week').all().map(i => i.json).filter(r => r.shifted).map(r => ({series: r.series_id, title: r.title, value: r.value, units: r.units, was: r.previous_regime, now: r.regime, quarter_move_pct: r.quarter_move_pct, year_move_pct: r.year_move_pct, streak: r.streak, streak_direction: r.streak_direction, z: r.z_score, note: r.note})), null, 1) }}

The rest of the watchlist, for context only:
{{ JSON.stringify($('Compare With Last Week').all().map(i => i.json).filter(r => r.usable && !r.shifted).map(r => ({series: r.series_id, value: r.value, units: r.units, regime: r.regime})), null, 1) }}

Write three to five sentences on what these shifts mean for this business specifically - demand, hiring, borrowing or pricing. Say which one matters most and why. If a shift is a technical artefact of a noisy series rather than a real turn, say so. Do not forecast and do not give investment advice. No preamble, no bullet points, no sign-off.

